{"name":"Tutu","hex":"#f8e4e3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tutu","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tutu"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tutu (clothing)","blocks":[{"text":"A tutu is a dress worn as a costume in a classical ballet performance, often with attached bodice. It may be made of tarlatan, muslin, silk, tulle, gauze, or nylon. Modern tutus have two basic types: the Romantic tutu is soft and bell-shaped, reaching the calf or ankle; the Classical tutu is short and stiff, projecting horizontally from the waist and hip."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Colourful_ballet_tutu.jpg/330px-Colourful_ballet_tutu.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tutu_(clothing)","wikidata":"Q1359804"},{"title":"Tutu (name)","blocks":[{"text":"Tutu is both a surname and a given name."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tutu_(name)","wikidata":"Q16915054"},{"title":"Tutu (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Tutu is a studio album by American jazz trumpeter, composer and bandleader Miles Davis, released on September 29, 1986, by Warner Bros. Records. The album is Miles Davis' tribute to Archbishop Desmond Tutu who was a human rights and anti-apartheid activist. It was recorded primarily at Capitol Studios in Los Angeles and Clinton Recording in New York, except the song \"Backyard Ritual\", which was recorded at Le Gonks in West Hollywood. Davis received the 1986 Best Jazz Instrumental Performance, Soloist Grammy Award for his performance on the album."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/06/Miles_Davis-Tutu_%28album_cover%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tutu_(album)","wikidata":"Q831324"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/AnnaPavlo